# Allowlist for check-public-artifact.sh, the maintainer's pre-publish leak
# sweep. That script is not part of this repository and nothing here runs it;
# an adopter can ignore this file.
#
# Every entry below names a file the workstream kit installs under .claude/
# and the fixture identifiers that file carries as examples or self-check
# strings. Entries are scoped to the file AND the identifier, never to a
# whole file, so a genuine leak in one of these files still reports. The
# sweep prints its suppression count on every run.

# The state-file format rule shows a task pointer, a backlog and a gate.
^\.claude/rules/workstreams-rule\.md:[0-9]+:.*#(DR-[0-9]|G-DR)\b
^\.claude/rules/workstreams-rule\.md:[0-9]+:.*#MG-2\b

# The workstream template ships the Completion phase as literal tasks.
^\.claude/skills/workstream-create/templates/workstream\.md:[0-9]+:.*#CL-[123]\b

# The state module's gloss pattern comment names the gate form it must
# not miss, with the kit workstream's own gate as the example.
^\.claude/scripts/workstream_state\.py:[0-9]+:.*#G-OG\b

# The record script's docstring and self-check strings quote fixture IDs
# as examples of the word-boundary and gloss rules.
^\.claude/scripts/workstream-record\.py:[0-9]+:.*#(G-(BD|OG)|(BD|OL|OG|EX)-[0-9]+[a-z]?)\b

# This file's own entries quote the identifiers they exempt; exempt by
# shape, a line whose content begins with the anchor every entry starts
# with. Comments here are not exempt.
^\.public-sweep-allow:[0-9]+:[-+ ]?\^
